1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:04,050
So who holds the pen?

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,350
I'm Max Geurtsen, and this is Purser.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:14,250
Three Claude agents, each with its own card and mandate.

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,850
The rails and the code hold the limits.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,555
An agent proposes.

6
00:00:19,605 --> 00:00:21,350
Rules in code check it.

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,850
Beyond the limits, a person signs.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,850
Airwallex or Metal moves the money, into the books.

9
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,987
On the third of November, three Claude

10
00:00:31,037 --> 00:00:33,750
agents ran a business, on test money.

11
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,450
Their supplier doubled its price, past the mandate's cap.

12
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,550
We let one through on purpose; Purser normally refuses first.

13
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,850
Metal refused it, on chain.

14
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,550
Our simulated customer disputed twelve orders.

15
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:49,850
All twelve were signed by its own agent.

16
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,750
Support refunded the three with wrong data.

17
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:54,034
The other nine?

18
00:00:54,084 --> 00:00:55,850
Rejected, with Face ID.

19
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,950
The Treasury agent planned a euro payment.

20
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,850
The phone shows the exact terms.

21
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:11,050
Six seconds from Face ID to paid.

22
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:14,150
In the sandbox, the settlement is simulated.

23
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:17,450
Every id is on the proof page.

24
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,553
Your turn: open your own test world, and

25
00:01:21,603 --> 00:01:23,850
sign with your own Face ID.

26
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,850
The server checks the signature against the exact terms.

27
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,650
Why Face ID, not a password?

28
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:39,236
A password is the same every time;

29
00:01:39,286 --> 00:01:41,576
Face ID signs these exact terms.

30
00:01:41,626 --> 00:01:43,550
Change anything: worthless.

31
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,750
All tests passing.

32
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,050
An audit log, hash-chained.

33
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,750
Metal refused one purchase over its

34
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,350
cap; the CFO rejected one proposal.

35
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,950
Twenty-four of twenty-four decisions by Claude.

36
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:01,750
Real: the Airwallex sandbox, Metal testnet, Claude, Face ID.

37
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:02,952
Ours or simulated:

38
00:02:03,002 --> 00:02:07,850
suppliers, customer, merchant, and the second approver, a labelled test passkey.

39
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:11,850
A price shock, a dispute, a euro bill.

40
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,661
Claude decided, the rails and the code held the

41
00:02:15,711 --> 00:02:19,450
limits, and I signed only what went beyond them.

42
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,550
Purser, Starter Kit 11.
